# Skill: GitHub X Latest Push

> A Grok skill that shows the latest GitHub push next to any related posts on X.

## Purpose
Explain the skill as a two-pane view: what just shipped on GitHub, and whether X mentioned it. Source: fitzyracing1/skill-github-x-latest-push.

## How it works (plain English)
1. Read the latest commit for the account.
2. Search X for matching posts.
3. Show both sides together.
4. Stay read-only unless a later ask says push.

## Key ideas
- Latest push (the newest commit)
- Related X posts (public mentions of that ship)
- Combined view (one answer, two sources)

## The actual code
```
# source: fitzyracing1/skill-github-x-latest-push
commit = latest_github_push()
posts = search_x(commit)
show(commit, posts)
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. latest_github_push() → “get the newest commit”
2. search_x(commit) → “look for matching posts”
3. show(...) → “put both in one view”

## Decisions the program makes
- If no commit exists → say so
- If no X posts exist → say none found

## What a person would notice
Ship and mention in one glance.

## Current status
Barrage clone.

## Next possible steps
Open the HTML skill and ask for the latest push.
